(Elderly and Cardiovascular Health Safety Protocol) Tj T*

(Document ID: REF-ELD-2024) Tj T*
(Source: Geriatric Health Council & Cardiovascular Protection Association) Tj T*
(Topic: Air Pollution Precautions for Seniors and Cardiac Patients) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Health Considerations:) Tj T*
(1. Fine Particulate Matter \(PM2.5\) penetrates deep into the bloodstream, triggering vascular inflammation and arrhythmia.) Tj T*
(2. Seniors with hypertension, coronary artery disease, or COPD are at elevated risk during particulate spikes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Safety Recommendations:) Tj T*
(- Monitor daily local AQI and particulate readings prior to outdoor plans.) Tj T*
(- When AQI exceeds 100, refrain from outdoor yard work, gardening, or long walks.) Tj T*
(- Keep emergency respiratory medication \(e.g. quick-relief inhalers\) accessible.) Tj T*
(- Maintain adequate hydration and remain in air-conditioned, HEPA-filtered indoor environments.) Tj T*
ET
